{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.skein_finiteness_bound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.skein_finiteness_bound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Fin"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.skein_finiteness_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.skein_finiteness_bound","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skein_finiteness_bound.lean#L76-L95","doc":"**Skein finiteness bound** (manuscript claims (i)–(iii)).\n\nThe number of stable nuclear configurations at a given substrate\nparameter `q` is **finite**.  The stability boundary is the zero locus\nof the Skein polynomial `P_{N(p,n)}(q) = ∏ᵢ V̂ᵢ(q)`, and a configuration\nis stable only if every per-generator traced volume is positive (whence\n`P > 0`).\n\nAll three sub-claims are *derived*:\n\n* (i) `P = ∏ᵢ V̂ᵢ`           (Skein factorisation, definitional);\n* (ii) `(∀ i, 0 < V̂ᵢ) → 0 < P`   (per-generator positivity ⇒ `P > 0`);\n* (iii) the configurations with mass number `≤ Amax` form a **finite**\n  set (finiteness of the stability window). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:skein-finiteness-bound","label":"prop:skein-finiteness-bound","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/skein-finiteness-bound.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.boundedConfigs_finite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.boundedConfigs_finite","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skein_finiteness_bound.lean#L58-L74","doc":"**Finiteness of stable configurations** (manuscript claim (iii)).\nFor any mass-number bound `Amax`, the set of configurations with\n`Z + N ≤ Amax` is finite.  Derived via the injection\n`c ↦ (c.Z, c.N) : Fin (Amax+1) × Fin (Amax+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.boundedConfigs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.boundedConfigs","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skein_finiteness_bound.lean#L53-L56","doc":"The bounded set of configurations whose mass number `A = Z + N` does\nnot exceed `Amax` (the physical stability window). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.instDecidableEqNuclearConfig.decEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.instDecidableEqNuclearConfig.decEq","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skein_finiteness_bound.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.instDecidableEqNuclearConfig","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.instDecidableEqNuclearConfig","kind":"instance","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skein_finiteness_bound.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NuclearConfig.N","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NuclearConfig.N","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skein_finiteness_bound.lean#L50-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NuclearConfig.Z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NuclearConfig.Z","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skein_finiteness_bound.lean#L49-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NuclearConfig.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NuclearConfig.mk","kind":"ctor","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skein_finiteness_bound.lean#L48-L48","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NuclearConfig","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NuclearConfig","kind":"structure","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skein_finiteness_bound.lean#L47-L51","doc":"A nuclear configuration: proton number `Z` and neutron number `N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.skeinPoly_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.skeinPoly_pos","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skein_finiteness_bound.lean#L40-L45","doc":"**Per-generator positivity criterion** (manuscript claim (ii)).\nIf every per-generator traced volume is positive, the Skein\npolynomial is positive.  Derived from `Finset.prod_pos`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.skeinPoly_eq_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.skeinPoly_eq_prod","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skein_finiteness_bound.lean#L35-L38","doc":"**Skein factorisation** (manuscript claim (i)).  `P = ∏ᵢ V̂ᵢ` —\ndefinitional (`rfl`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.skeinPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.skeinPoly","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/skein_finiteness_bound.lean#L30-L33","doc":"The Skein polynomial of an `A`-nucleon configuration at fixed `q` is\nthe product of the `A − 1` per-generator traced volumes `V̂ᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}